<%#
  One banded section of the organization card: a tinted heading strip, then its fields as a
  two-column `<dl>`. Locals: `title`.

  The band is the line item card's pattern -- `border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50` -- which marks
  a change of kind. It replaces six bare `<hr>` elements that rendered in **slate-900**, because an
  unstyled `<hr>` inherits `currentColor` under preflight, so the page carried six near-black rules
  where every other divider in the app is a slate-200 hairline.

  One gap number, `gap-y-4`, against the seven different gaps this had before. Two columns rather
  than four: the labels in the approval and request sections are long enough that four would wrap
  every one of them.
%>
<%# `py-4` on every band including the last. It used to drop to `pt-4` on the final one, on the
    assumption that the card supplied the bottom padding -- it does not, because the card is
    rendered `padded: false` so its body has none at all. The last field of "Annual survey" sat
    **1px** from the card's bottom edge while the seven bands above it had 16. %>
<h3 class="border-y border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 first:border-t-0">
  <%= title %>
</h3>
<div class="px-5 py-4">
  <dl class="grid gap-x-6 gap-y-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><%= yield %></dl>
</div>
